WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.647
Post an opening once.

00:00:01.647 --> 00:00:05.439
Volunteers nearby who care about your cause swipe right.

00:00:05.439 --> 00:00:09.630
You say yes, and after the shift one tap confirms their hours.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.295
A nonprofit joins first.

00:00:12.295 --> 00:00:17.240
Jordan asks for access with the organization's name and tax ID.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.886
A Causematch admin checks every request.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:24.870
Then Jordan signs in from an emailed link, no password.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.907
Jordan says the nonprofit confirms hours, then posts an opening.

00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:32.350
That's the whole form, written once.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.503
Now, a volunteer.

00:00:35.503 --> 00:00:40.142
Riley signs up with an email address and opens the link we send.

00:00:40.142 --> 00:00:41.070
No password.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:47.990
One short form: a first name, where Riley will help from, and how much they care about each cause.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.913
Riley ticks the times they're usually free, like Saturday mornings.

00:00:54.913 --> 00:00:56.200
These stay private.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.919
Riley needs hours confirmed for school.

00:01:00.919 --> 00:01:05.590
One checkbox, and the deck shows only nonprofits that confirm them.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:13.341
Jordan's opening comes first: close by, on a Saturday morning Riley is free, and it confirms hours.

00:01:13.341 --> 00:01:14.839
Riley taps the heart.

00:01:14.839 --> 00:01:18.380
A like becomes a match when the nonprofit says yes.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:22.007
On Jordan's side, the inbox badge goes up.

00:01:22.007 --> 00:01:25.360
Riley appears with only what they chose to share.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.825
Jordan accepts and says hi.

00:01:27.825 --> 00:01:32.510
The first shift is booked, and on Riley's phone, right there: it's a match.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:38.060
Riley taps Say hi on the match, reads Jordan's message, and replies.

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:44.280
The reply arrives live, and Jordan's dashboard flags it as a message to answer.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.378
The shift is on Jordan's schedule.

00:01:47.378 --> 00:01:53.800
After it happens, Jordan marks Riley as attended in one tap, with the hours already filled in.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:02:01.440
Back on Riley's phone, the hours Jordan confirmed are there: the shift, the nonprofit, and who confirmed them.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:11.650
Riley gets a certificate for Silver Lake Garden Friends: every confirmed shift, the total, a signature code, and a PDF with a QR code.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:16.869
Anyone with the link can check that it's genuine, with no sign-in.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:20.810
Same nonprofit, same total, unchanged since it was issued.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.428
Causematch.

00:02:22.428 --> 00:02:24.586
Nonprofits post and say yes.

00:02:24.586 --> 00:02:25.926
Volunteers swipe.

00:02:25.926 --> 00:02:28.530
Join the Los Angeles County pilot.
